read that state as merged. There is no v2; v1 is the only revision.

WHO THIS AFFECTS HERE: every board whose pmic-glink node declares
"qcom,sm8550-pmic-glink", which the driver maps to QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550 and
which takes the same probe branch as the SM8350 fallback. That is all thirteen
qcs8550 boards (via qcs8550-ayaneo-pocket-common.dtsi and qcs8550-ayn-common.dtsi)
plus both sm8650 boards, Pocket S2 and Pocket FIT (via sm8650-ayaneo-common.dtsi).
The six sm8250 boards -- Pocket Max among them -- have no pmic-glink node at all;
they use qcom_pm8150b_charger + qcom_fg (patch 0072) and are untouched either way.

NO REGRESSION RISK from flipping the unit: neither sm8350_bat_props[] nor
sm8550_bat_props[] exposes any POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ENERGY_*, so the mWh side of
those unit guards was unreachable on this path to begin with. The only change
visible to userspace is CHARGE_FULL / CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN / CHARGE_EMPTY going
from -ENODATA to a real value.

DROP THIS PATCH once it lands in the pinned stable series -- grep
qcom_battmgr_probe() for "battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh" on the next bump.

---

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1690,6 +1690,14 @@
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(battmgr->wls_psy),
 					     "failed to register wireless charing power supply\n");
 	} else {
+		/*
+		 * The SM8350-class firmware has no BATTMGR_BAT_INFO request, so
+		 * @unit is never populated from the firmware. It reports charge
+		 * domain values, so set it statically here - otherwise the
+		 * CHARGE_* properties are rejected with -ENODATA.
+		 */
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
 			psy_desc = &sm8550_bat_psy_desc;
 		else
